    <%- include('../partials/policy-reviewed') %>

    <h2>General information only</h2>
    <p>The pages on this site about conditions, treatments and recovery are written to help you understand your options and prepare for a visit. They're general. They can't take account of your age, your health, your medicines or the details of your injury.</p>
    <p>Nothing on this site is a diagnosis or a treatment plan for you. Only a doctor who has examined you can give you that.</p>

    <h2>Don't delay seeing a doctor</h2>
    <p>Don't put off seeing a doctor, and don't stop a treatment you've been given, because of something you read here. If you're worried about a symptom, <a href="/appointment">ask for an appointment</a> or see a doctor near you.</p>

    <h2>Emergencies</h2>
    <p>This website and its appointment form aren't for emergencies. Go to the nearest hospital emergency department if you have a serious injury, a bone showing through the skin, a limb that is badly bent, loss of feeling or movement, or loss of bladder or bowel control with back pain.</p>

    <h2>Results differ</h2>
    <p>Recovery times and results on these pages are typical ranges. Yours may be shorter or longer. Every operation carries risk, and no treatment works for everyone. Your surgeon will explain what you can expect before you decide on anything.</p>

    <h2>Who checks our pages</h2>
    <p>Each medical page is read and approved by a doctor at the clinic. The reviewer's name and the review date are at the foot of the page.</p>
  </div>
</section>

